{
  "conclusion": "A decoy credential for ci-vault was used twice on 2026-10-19 but the actor is not identified in the recorded evidence. Treat co-located real credentials as exposed: review access to the decoy's placement and rotate real credentials while keeping the decoy in place to detect reuse.",
  "observed_facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Open finding f-1x9apv9xn9jsp claims a registered decoy credential placed with ci-vault was used 2 times, with first_seen 2026-10-19T15:00:00Z and last_seen 2026-10-19T15:04:00Z, severity high, outcome_state attempted, evidence_level source_reported.",
      "evidence": ["f-1x9apv9xn9jsp", "ci-vault", "ev-9tqzdm1mz3xo6", "ev-j471unsvb0x7"]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both supporting events show action decoy_used with outcome attempted from deception service, with attempted_operation list_objects then get_object, both with the same client_ip.",
      "evidence": ["ev-9tqzdm1mz3xo6", "ev-j471unsvb0x7", "src-8954"]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The finding record explicitly states the person or system that used the decoy is not identified and use of the decoy does not show where an intrusion began, and lists coverage gap for how the credential was obtained.",
      "evidence": ["f-1x9apv9xn9jsp"]
    },
    {
      "statement": "ci-vault is a storage asset in staging with an incoming reads_from relationship from inventory-svc; guidance states to not deploy new secrets to the decoy's placement until rotation completes and to treat co-located real credentials as exposed.",
      "evidence": ["ci-vault", "inventory-svc", "f-1x9apv9xn9jsp"]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Telemetry coverage shows deception service and sign-in log healthy, while inventory-svc has no telemetry and is unobserved.",
      "evidence": ["src-8954", "src-b920", "inventory-svc", "sso-gateway"]
    }
  ],
  "interpretations": [
    {
      "statement": "The shared client_ip alone does not identify who did this; it could be NAT, VPN, or spoofed infrastructure and is not correlated to an account in the evidence.",
      "based_on": ["ev-9tqzdm1mz3xo6", "ev-j471unsvb0x7", "f-1x9apv9xn9jsp"],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sequence of list_objects followed 4 minutes later by get_object is consistent with discovery then attempted retrieval, but outcome attempted means successful exfiltration is not shown.",
      "based_on": ["ev-9tqzdm1mz3xo6", "ev-j471unsvb0x7", "f-1x9apv9xn9jsp"],
      "confidence": "medium"
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lack of telemetry for inventory-svc, which reads from ci-vault, limits ability to rule out adjacent access or misuse.",
      "based_on": ["inventory-svc", "ci-vault", "src-8954", "src-b920"],
      "confidence": "medium"
    }
  ],
  "gaps": [
    {
      "statement": "How the decoy credential was obtained and initial entry point is unknown per the finding.",
      "kind": "missing"
    },
    {
      "statement": "No account, identity, or system attribution is present in the returned events; client_ip is the only network indicator.",
      "kind": "insufficient"
    },
    {
      "statement": "No telemetry for inventory-svc, so activity from a service that reads ci-vault is not visible.",
      "kind": "incomplete"
    },
    {
      "statement": "Correlation with sign-in log around 14:58-15:04Z has not been established in the evidence bundle.",
      "kind": "incomplete"
    }
  ],
  "next_steps": [
    "Review access to where the decoy was placed to determine who could have obtained it, including ci-vault ACLs and any repo/ticket/log exposure.",
    "List and rotate real credentials co-located with the decoy, redeploy consumers, and do not deploy new secrets to that placement until rotation completes.",
    "Keep the decoy in place and monitor for reuse; correlate sso-gateway sign-in logs and any ci-vault audit logs around 2026-10-19T15:00-15:04Z.",
    "Investigate inventory-svc access to ci-vault via out-of-band logs since it has no Digital Kingdom telemetry, and restore audit coverage if possible."
  ],
  "requires_authorization": [
    "secrets.rotate_credentials: rotate real credentials stored alongside the used decoy",
    "data.restrict_access: temporarily narrow which identities can read ci-vault",
    "Any edge block, rate-limit, forced re-auth, or privilege revert related to this alert requires separate human approval; Digital Kingdom never executes containment."
  ]
}

